# Both findings live under /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages, the
# *system* Python bundled in the pinned python:3.11-slim base image (see
# docker/Dockerfile's PYTHON_BASE_IMAGE comment). The app runs out of
# /opt/venv, which PATH puts first, so this copy of pip/setuptools/wheel is
# never invoked at runtime. Not fixable from this repo without patching the
# base image directly; Dependabot's docker ecosystem entry will flag base
# image bumps that may resolve these upstream.

# setuptools' vendored jaraco.context — path traversal via malicious tar archives
CVE-2026-23949

# setuptools' vendored wheel — code execution via malicious wheel file
CVE-2026-24049

# Both findings below come from pip's own internal `pip/_vendor/vendor.txt`
# manifest (present in both /opt/venv and the system Python's site-packages
# — every pip install ships this), which trivy's python-pkg analyzer parses
# as if it were a real installed-package lockfile. Confirmed by inspecting
# the built image directly, not just trusting the report:
#
# - GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 (msgpack 1.1.2): real, but it's pip's own private
#   vendored copy at pip/_vendor/msgpack/, used only by pip's internal
#   CacheControl HTTP-response caching during `pip install`/`pip download`
#   — never imported by this app (which uses the real top-level `msgpack`
#   package, separately installed and pinned to 1.2.1 in requirements.txt).
#   Not fixable from here: checked pip's latest release directly against
#   its GitHub source (pypa/pip@26.2, the newest available on PyPI as of
#   this check) and it still vendors msgpack 1.1.2 — no pip release exists
#   yet with a fixed vendored copy.
# - CVE-2025-47273 (setuptools 70.3.0): a straight false positive, not a
#   real risk being accepted. vendor.txt lists this as a reference/pinned
#   version note; pip does not actually vendor a setuptools package_index.py
#   (the vulnerable module) anywhere — verified no such file exists in the
#   image. The real, fully separate setuptools installs (venv and system)
#   are both upgraded to 83.0.0 in docker/Dockerfile.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
